-- Criminal Damage Act 1971 (1971 c. 48), England and Wales.
-- NOUNS ONLY: the things, persons, facts and classifications that the other
-- modules of this encoding speak about. No rules, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT here.
--
-- Source: ukpga-1971-48.txt, a plain-text rendering (not the official text) of
-- the legislation.gov.uk revised text, version 2008-10-01.
--
-- The test for what lives here: could a witness of ordinary competence testify
-- to this fact, or does answering it need the Act? Only the first kind is a
-- field below. Whether a thing is "property", whether it "belongs to another",
-- whether a person has "a lawful excuse" are the Act's own questions: they are
-- worked out by rules in the other modules from the facts declared here.
--
-- Field names are affirmative (no "not", no "did not"), because a negated field
-- name plus a NOT in the rule is a double negative that no diagnostic finds.
-- Words of state of mind or judgment ("intending", "reckless", "believed")
-- are BOOLEAN facts that the person states; the Act defines none of them and
-- this encoding does not decide any of them for anyone.
--
-- The person charged is "the accused" throughout the field names; the Act says
-- "he" and "himself".

§ `The Criminal Damage Act 1971 -- nouns`

§§ `The thing (section 10(1))`

-- s 10(1): "property" means property of a tangible nature, whether real or
-- personal, including money, (a) including wild creatures which have been
-- tamed or are ordinarily kept in captivity, and any other wild creatures or
-- their carcasses if, but only if, they have been reduced into possession
-- which has not been lost or abandoned or are in the course of being reduced
-- into possession; but (b) not including mushrooms growing wild on any land or
-- flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant growing wild on any land.
DECLARE Thing HAS
    `of a tangible nature` IS A BOOLEAN                                          -- s 10(1): can be touched; real (land, buildings) or personal (goods)
    `money` IS A BOOLEAN                                                          -- s 10(1): "including money"
    `a wild creature tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN         -- s 10(1)(a), first limb
    `any other wild creature, or the carcass of a wild creature` IS A BOOLEAN    -- s 10(1)(a), second limb
    `reduced into possession which has not been lost or abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(a): only read for the second limb
    `in the course of being reduced into possession` IS A BOOLEAN                -- s 10(1)(a): only read for the second limb
    `a mushroom, including any fungus, growing wild on any land` IS A BOOLEAN    -- s 10(1)(b) and the last sentence of s 10(1)
    `flowers, fruit or foliage of a plant, including a shrub or tree, growing wild on any land` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(b) and the last sentence of s 10(1)

§§ `One person's connection with property (section 10(2) to (4))`

-- s 10(2)(b): "having in it any proprietary right or interest (not being an
-- equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an
-- interest)". Three mutually exclusive positions, so one choice and not two flags.
DECLARE `Interest in property` IS ONE OF
    `no proprietary right or interest`
    `a proprietary right or interest`
    `only an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest`

-- s 10(2) to (4): the ways in which property is "treated for the purposes of
-- this Act as belonging to" a person. One record is one person's connection.
DECLARE Connection HAS
    `custody or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN                                            -- s 10(2)(a)
    `interest in it` IS A `Interest in property`                                       -- s 10(2)(b)
    `a charge on it` IS A BOOLEAN                                                      -- s 10(2)(c)
    `a right to enforce a trust to which it is subject` IS A BOOLEAN                   -- s 10(3)
    `the corporation sole whose property it is, whether or not there is a vacancy in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(4)

-- The property in question and who is connected with it. "Another" in the Act
-- is a person other than the accused (see NOTES.md, fork register).
DECLARE `Property facts` HAS
    `the thing` IS A Thing
    `the accused's connection with it` IS A Connection
    `other persons' connections with it` IS A LIST OF Connection                      -- one entry per person other than the accused

§§ `What is done to the property (sections 1 to 3, 10(5))`

-- In section 1 this is what was done; in section 2 what was threatened; in
-- section 3 what the thing in custody was intended to be used to do.
DECLARE Damage HAS
    `destruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- "destroy or damage", in the ordinary sense, before s 10(5) is applied
    `by a modification of the contents of a computer or computer storage medium alone` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10(5)
    `with an effect that impairs the physical condition of the computer or computer storage medium` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(5)

§§ `Beliefs and lawful excuse (section 5)`

-- s 5(3): "it is immaterial whether a belief is justified or not if it is
-- honestly held". A belief is therefore two facts, and the rule reads only one.
DECLARE Belief HAS
    `honestly held` IS A BOOLEAN
    `justified` IS A BOOLEAN                                                          -- s 5(3): never read by any rule; carried so that the immateriality is visible

-- s 5(2)(a) and (b), and the residual in s 5(2) ("whether or not he would be
-- treated ... as having a lawful excuse apart from this subsection") and s 5(5).
DECLARE `Lawful excuse facts` HAS
    `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS A Belief                                            -- s 5(2)(a), first limb
    `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS A Belief  -- s 5(2)(a), second limb
    `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS A BOOLEAN                                                  -- s 5(2)(b)
    `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN                                                               -- s 5(2)(b)
    `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN         -- s 5(4) widens "right or interest in property"
    `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS A BOOLEAN                                                          -- s 5(2)(b): "which was ... vested"
    `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS A Belief                                               -- s 5(2)(b): "or which he believed to be vested"
    `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS A Belief                                      -- s 5(2)(b)(i)
    `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS A Belief  -- s 5(2)(b)(ii)
    `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN                                                -- s 5(2) opening words, s 5(5)

§§ `The offences (sections 1 to 3)`

-- The offences, one constructor for each limb that the Act treats differently.
-- Section 5(1) tells the limbs under sections 2 and 3 apart, section 4 tells
-- arson apart from the rest, so the limbs below are the finest grain either needs.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`
    `arson under section 1(1)`
    `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`
    `arson under section 1(2)`
    `an offence under section 2(a)`                                              -- a threat to damage property belonging to the person threatened or a third person
    `an offence under section 2(b)`                                              -- a threat to damage the accused's own property in a way known to be likely to endanger life
    `an offence under section 3(a)`                                              -- having a thing intending to use it to damage property belonging to some other person
    `an offence under section 3(b)`                                              -- having a thing intending to use it to damage the accused's or the user's property in a way known to be likely to endanger life

-- s 1(1) and s 1(2): destroying or damaging property.
DECLARE `Section 1 facts` HAS
    `the property` IS A `Property facts`
    `the damage` IS A Damage
    `the destruction or damage was by fire` IS A BOOLEAN                              -- s 1(3)
    `intending to destroy or damage any such property` IS A BOOLEAN                   -- s 1(1): "such" = belonging to another
    `reckless as to whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 1(1)
    `intending to destroy or damage any property` IS A BOOLEAN                        -- s 1(2)(a): any property, whoever it belongs to
    `reckless as to whether any property would be destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 1(2)(a)
    `intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 1(2)(b)
    `reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered` IS A BOOLEAN          -- s 1(2)(b)
    `lawful excuse` IS A `Lawful excuse facts`

-- s 2: threats to destroy or damage property.
DECLARE `Section 2 facts` HAS
    `a threat made to another` IS A BOOLEAN                                           -- s 2: "makes to another a threat"
    `intending that that other would fear it would be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN       -- s 2
    `the property threatened` IS A `Property facts`
    `the threatened damage` IS A Damage
    `knowing it likely that the threatened destruction or damage would endanger the life of that other or a third person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2(b)
    `lawful excuse` IS A `Lawful excuse facts`

-- s 3: possessing anything with intent to destroy or damage property.
DECLARE `Section 3 facts` HAS
    `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3: "has anything in his custody or under his control"
    `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3
    `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged` IS A `Property facts`
    `the intended damage` IS A Damage
    `the user's connection with the property` IS A Connection                        -- s 3(b): "the user's property"; the accused's own connection if the accused is to be the user
    `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(b)
    `lawful excuse` IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
